From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui/cocoa: start animation, then Omarchy's logo until the desktop

What: when the window opens, OMACVM turns into Omarchy's logo (O, M and A
stay, the cells of C, V and M fly and land as R, C, H and Y), Omarchy green
on Omarchy's background: OMACVM holds 0.6 s, the cells fly for about 2.6 s,
the glow goes by 3.56 s. Then the logo holds until Omarchy's desktop (or its
login or lock screen) is there, over the firmware's progress bar, GRUB's
text and Linux's console, and fades into it. The desktop is there when the
guest's picture is lit almost everywhere (a wallpaper, not text on black nor
Hyprland's grey before the wallpaper; 32 x 18 pixels looked at 4 times a
second, read back from the scanout's texture), or 2 s after Omarchy's
display agent (omacvm-displays, a user service that starts with the desktop)
said hello on its port org.omacvm.display without a lit picture (a dark
wallpaper). The hello comes about 0.5 s before the wallpaper: fading on it
showed Hyprland's grey for a moment. QEMU's window talks to the agent when
the launcher sets OMACVM_DISPLAY_SOCKET; without that channel the port's
opening counts (with it, the firmware opens the port too, EDK2's
VirtioSerialDxe answers the host's open 0.2 s into the boot). If the
desktop comes before the animation ends, the animation still plays to its
end. The logo gives way at once when the VM stops on an error, and after
40 s of running time without a desktop (OMACVM_SPLASH_HOLD_SECONDS), so a
prompt or an error in the guest is not hidden for long; qemu.log says which
it was. After that it still looks once a second for the desktop, so that
an output the desktop turns off later is black, not the logo. The
animation's frames come from a display link, which gives a window that is
not visible none: once the animation is over by the clock and no frame came
for 0.25 s, the logo fades without them (it stayed over the desktop). After a reboot the logo comes back, still, the same way. Reduce
motion or OMACVM_SPLASH_ANIMATION=0: the logo without the morph. Only the
main window has the animation.
Under it, in the GL layers of the main window and the other displays' windows:
until the guest shows a picture on an output, and when it switches it off,
Omarchy's logo on Omarchy's background instead of QEMU's placeholder text
("Display output is not active.", "Guest has not initialized the display
(yet)."); once the desktop was there (until the next reset), plain black, as
a screen that is off (an idle Omarchy turns its display off). If the guest
has shown nothing of its own 90 s of running time after it started
(OMACVM_SPLASH_HINT_SECONDS), a line under the logo says Omarchy is taking
long and where its logs are (OMACVM_LOGS, set by the launcher), and qemu.log
gets a warning. OMACVM_BOOT_SPLASH=0 brings QEMU's text back and turns the
logo and the animation off. The main window's layer now draws again when the
window changes size (cheap; the still logo has no frames of its own).
With frames shown as IOSurfaces (the default since 2.9.0) the still logo
and the black are drawn into the surface at the view's size in pixels
(updateUIInfo tells it, and a new size draws again), and the animation's
layer goes over the surface layer as it did over the CAOpenGLLayer;
OMACVM_GL_PRESENT=layer draws them in the CAOpenGLLayer as before. The patch comes after the GPU,
shortcut, pointer and idle-refresh patches of ui/cocoa.m.

Why: every start showed QEMU's text for a few seconds (before the firmware,
and from GRUB until Linux draws), then the firmware, GRUB and Linux's text,
and every reboot the text for longer. It looked like errors but is just the
guest getting ready. The user asked for the logo from the window's first
frame to the desktop, and for the animation (the preview they picked,
a-pixel-morph) to run slower to fill the 3 to 5 s of loading.

How: the animation and the held logo are a Core Animation layer over the
window's GL layer (a shape layer for the cells, sharp at any size and scale;
a small glow image under them laid over the preview's frame), driven by a
CADisplayLink on the main thread; the guest is never held up. Their green and
navy are made in the window's colour space: GL's pixels reach the screen
unconverted, so the layer's are the very values of the GL logo, the
firmware's and the guest's. The core (no Cocoa, no QEMU, ui/omacvm-splash.h)
is a port of the preview's generator on a slowed timeline: the flying cells'
table is made by boot-logo/make-splash-morph.py, the glow is the preview's
blur (Pillow's resampling weights). The still logo in the GL layers is an
81 x 19 texture with sharp cells. The logo is as big as the firmware's
1920 x 1080 frame stretched to the view would have it (810 x 190 there:
10 pixels a cell; the user asked for a small logo, about 200 pixels tall),
with square cells, in the middle. The logo is the firmware's
(boot-logo/make-logo-bmp.py logo.svg --rows, from Omarchy's logo.svg, MIT).

Upstream: OmacVM only (branding), not for QEMU.

Test: Tests/display/test-boot-splash-cells.py (the cells make exactly the
firmware's Logo.bmp of edk2-logo-omarchy.patch, at SPLASH_CELL);
make-splash-morph.py --check (the table is the generator's);
Tests/display/test-boot-splash-morph.c (the core starts as OMACVM, holds it
about 0.6 s, flies 2.5 to 3 s and ends as the logo, still, on the pixels GL's
nearest sampling gives at several window sizes, square cells; no jumps; the
glow comes and goes; the desktop is told apart from the firmware's logo,
a console full of text and Hyprland's grey; the logo goes on the lit
desktop, not on the agent's hello alone, 2 s after the hello at most, at
the time limit only without the agent, at once on an error); Tests/display/
test-boot-splash-fade.m (the layer's no-action list has "opacity", so the
fade into the desktop is only its own 0.4 s one: CA's implicit 0.25 s fade
ended first and the logo came back at ~25 %). The build runs all four;
Tests/display/check-boot-splash.sh runs them from this patch alone (CI).
The core's cells and glow at any time are the earlier core's (which matched
the preview's frames) at the preview's time, frame for frame at 120 Hz.
Checked in the app on a test VM: a cold start (OMACVM 0.6 s, the morph to
about 3.2 s at ~60 fps, the logo held over the firmware, GRUB's menu and
Linux, given way when the wallpaper showed, 12.6 s), a reboot (the still
logo again to the desktop), the display agent's port opened by hand (gives
way at once), the time limit at 2 s (the animation still ends first), the
still logo; the layer's green and navy are the GL logo's and the firmware's
values on the screen (168,205,118 and 26,27,38), the logo's box the GL
logo's to the pixel. Through the launcher (RC2 pre-stage verify) the
logo gave way 0.2 s in, on the firmware's port open: fixed by the hello.
RC2 polish: the fade landed on Hyprland's grey ~0.5 s before the wallpaper
(the logo now waits for it), and after a 40 s fallback an output the later
desktop turned off showed the logo instead of black. Twice in five test
starts the window got no display-link frames, the animation stood still
and the logo never faded: now it fades by the clock.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -210,6 +210,10 @@ static void cocoa_gl_switch(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
                             DisplaySurface *new_surface);
 
 static void cocoa_gl_render(void);
+/* OmacVM boot splash: the main view's size in pixels (BQL). */
+static void omacvm_splash_view_size(uint32_t w, uint32_t h);
+/* GL frames are shown as IOSurfaces (the view's layer is a plain CALayer). */
+static bool cocoa_gl_present_on(void);
 
 static bool cocoa_gl_is_compatible_dcl(DisplayGLCtx *dgc,
                                        DisplayChangeListener *dcl);
@@ -238,6 +242,8 @@ static DisplayGLCtx dgc = {
     self = [super init];
     if (self) {
         [self setAsynchronous:NO];
+        /* OmacVM: drawn again at the new size (the boot splash has no frames). */
+        [self setNeedsDisplayOnBoundsChange:YES];
     }
     return self;
 }
@@ -1266,6 +1272,9 @@ static bool omacvm_notch_mode(void)
     info.yoff = 0;
     NSSize backingFrameSize = [self convertSizeToBacking:frameSize];
     CGFloat backingScale = [[self window] backingScaleFactor];
+#ifdef CONFIG_OPENGL
+    omacvm_splash_view_size(backingFrameSize.width, backingFrameSize.height);
+#endif
     /* Keep the corresponding Hyprland logical dimensions integral. */
     uint32_t cleanScaleDivisor = backingScale > 1.75 ? 2 :
                                  backingScale > 1.25 ? 3 : 1;
@@ -3353,6 +3362,822 @@ static void cocoa_gl_destroy_context(DisplayGLCtx *dgc, QEMUGLContext ctx)
     CGLDestroyContext(ctx);
 }
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM boot splash. When the window opens, OMACVM turns into Omarchy's
+ * logo (the start animation, below), and the logo stays over the window
+ * until Omarchy's desktop (or its login or lock screen) is there: the
+ * firmware's progress bar, GRUB's text and Linux's console stay under it.
+ * After a reboot the logo comes back, still, the same way. The desktop is
+ * there when the guest's picture is lit almost everywhere
+ * (omacvm_splash_desktop: a wallpaper, not text on black nor Hyprland's grey
+ * before the wallpaper), looked at 4 times a second, or 2 s after Omarchy's
+ * display agent (omacvm-displays, a user service that starts with the
+ * desktop) said hello on its port, org.omacvm.display, without a lit
+ * picture (a dark wallpaper). QEMU's window talks to the agent when the
+ * launcher gives OMACVM_DISPLAY_SOCKET; else the port's opening counts. The
+ * hello comes about 0.5 s before the wallpaper, so the logo does not fade
+ * into Hyprland's grey (omacvm_splash_look decides).
+ * The logo gives way earlier, and says why in qemu.log, when the VM stops on
+ * an error (at once, even mid-animation), or when there is no desktop after
+ * OMACVM_SPLASH_HOLD_SECONDS (40) of running time: whatever the guest shows
+ * then (a prompt, an error) is not hidden for longer. It still looks once a
+ * second for the desktop then, so that an output the desktop turns off later
+ * is black, not the logo. If QEMU itself fails (no disk, a crash), it quits
+ * and the app says so, as before.
+ *
+ * Under the logo, in the window's GL layer, and on the other displays: until
+ * the guest shows a picture on an output, and when it switches the output
+ * off again, the output shows Omarchy's logo on Omarchy's background instead
+ * of QEMU's "Display output is not active."; once the desktop was there
+ * (until the next reset) plain black, as a screen that is off (an idle
+ * Omarchy turns its display off). When the guest has shown nothing of its own
+ * OMACVM_SPLASH_HINT_SECONDS (90) of running time after it started, a line
+ * under the logo says so and where the logs are, and qemu.log gets a warning.
+ * OMACVM_BOOT_SPLASH=0: QEMU's text, as before, and no animation.
+ *
+ * The logo is as big as the firmware's 1920 x 1080 frame stretched to the
+ * view would have it (810 x 190 there), with square cells, in the middle.
+ *
+ * Threads: the state below is used with the BQL (QEMU's thread, and the
+ * layers' draws on the main thread take it); the hint label and the
+ * animation's layer are main thread only.
+ */
+#include "hw/virtio/virtio-serial.h"
+#include "ui/omacvm-splash.h"   /* the logo's cells, the animation's core */
+
+static int omacvm_splash_on = -1;       /* OMACVM_BOOT_SPLASH */
+static GLuint omacvm_splash_tex;        /* the logo; gl_view_ctx's group */
+static bool omacvm_guest_drew;          /* a picture of the guest's since the last reset */
+static bool omacvm_desktop_up;          /* its desktop since the last reset */
+/* The display agent said hello since the last reset (main thread sets, BQL clears; atomic). */
+static bool omacvm_display_hello;
+static bool omacvm_splash_hint_up;
+static QEMUTimer *omacvm_splash_timer;
+static NSTextField *omacvm_splash_hint; /* main thread */
+/* The main scanout's place in its texture (the texture may not know its size). */
+static uint32_t gl_scanout_x, gl_scanout_y, gl_scanout_w, gl_scanout_h;
+/* The window's logo waits for the desktop: */
+static bool omacvm_overlay_ok;          /* the window has the logo's layer */
+static bool omacvm_holding;
+static bool omacvm_hold_dirty;          /* the guest's picture changed since the last look */
+static int64_t omacvm_hold_since;       /* QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL ms */
+static int64_t omacvm_agent_since = -1; /* QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME ms the agent was first seen, -1 */
+/* After the time limit the logo has gone; the desktop may still come (then black when off). */
+static bool omacvm_watching;
+static QEMUTimer *omacvm_hold_timer;    /* QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME, while holding or watching */
+/* The main view in pixels: the IOSurface path draws the logo at its size. */
+static uint32_t omacvm_view_w, omacvm_view_h;
+
+#define SPLASH_HOLD_TICK_MS 250
+#define SPLASH_SETTLE_TICK_MS 100   /* the agent is up: the wallpaper is close */
+#define SPLASH_WATCH_TICK_MS 1000   /* after the time limit */
+
+static bool omacvm_splash_enabled(void)
+{
+    if (omacvm_splash_on < 0) {
+        const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_BOOT_SPLASH");
+        omacvm_splash_on = !(v && !strcmp(v, "0"));
+        info_report("cocoa: boot splash %s",
+                    omacvm_splash_on ? "on" : "off (OMACVM_BOOT_SPLASH=0)");
+    }
+    return omacvm_splash_on;
+}
+
+/* An output without a picture of the guest's: none yet, or switched off. */
+static bool omacvm_splash_wanted(DisplayGLTextureBorrower borrow,
+                                 DisplaySurface *s)
+{
+#ifdef CONFIG_EGL
+    if (egl_surface) {
+        return false;   /* the logo's texture is in the CGL contexts */
+    }
+#endif
+    return !borrow && (!s || surface_is_placeholder(s)) &&
+           omacvm_splash_enabled();
+}
+
+/* BQL: the main view's size changed; the IOSurface path draws again at it. */
+static void omacvm_splash_view_size(uint32_t w, uint32_t h)
+{
+    if (w == omacvm_view_w && h == omacvm_view_h) {
+        return;
+    }
+    omacvm_view_w = w;
+    omacvm_view_h = h;
+    gl_dirty = true;
+    cocoa_refresh_activity();
+}
+
+/*
+ * With the BQL, in a CGL context that shares gl_view_ctx's objects: a w x h
+ * pixel output without a picture. logo: the logo on Omarchy's background;
+ * else black (the desktop was there: the guest turned the output off).
+ * top_first: the framebuffer's first row is the top (an IOSurface), not the
+ * bottom (a CAOpenGLLayer); gls: the context's shader.
+ */
+static void omacvm_splash_draw_with(QemuGLShader *gls, int w, int h, bool logo,
+                                    bool top_first)
+{
+    uint32_t bg = logo ? SPLASH_NAVY : 0;
+
+    glClearColor((bg >> 16) / 255.0, ((bg >> 8) & 0xff) / 255.0, (bg & 0xff) / 255.0, 1);
+    glClear(GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);
+    if (!logo) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_splash_tex) {
+        static uint32_t px[SPLASH_ROWS * SPLASH_COLS];
+        for (int r = 0; r < SPLASH_ROWS; r++) {
+            for (int c = 0; c < SPLASH_COLS; c++) {
+                px[r * SPLASH_COLS + c] = 0xff000000 |
+                    (omacvm_splash_cells[r][c] == '#' ? SPLASH_GREEN : SPLASH_NAVY);
+            }
+        }
+        glGenTextures(1, &omacvm_splash_tex);
+        glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, omacvm_splash_tex);
+        glPixelStorei(GL_UNPACK_ROW_LENGTH, 0);
+        glPixelStorei(GL_UNPACK_ALIGNMENT, 4);
+        glTexImage2D(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, GL_RGBA8, SPLASH_COLS, SPLASH_ROWS, 0,
+                     GL_BGRA, GL_UNSIGNED_INT_8_8_8_8_REV, px);
+        glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_S, GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
+        glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_T, GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
+    }
+    IntroGeom g = omacvm_intro_geom(w, h);
+
+    glViewport((int)g.left, top_first ? (int)g.top : h - (int)g.top - g.lh, g.lw, g.lh);
+    glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, omacvm_splash_tex);
+    /* Sharp cells, whatever the zoom filter. */
+    glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+    glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+    qemu_gl_run_texture_blit(gls, top_first);
+    glViewport(0, 0, w, h);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_splash_draw(int w, int h, bool logo)
+{
+    omacvm_splash_draw_with(dgc.gls, w, h, logo, false);
+}
+
+/* Main thread: the hint under the logo of the main window. */
+static void omacvm_splash_hint_show(bool show)
+{
+    if (!show) {
+        [omacvm_splash_hint removeFromSuperview];
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_splash_hint) {
+        const char *logs = getenv("OMACVM_LOGS");
+        NSString *text = logs && *logs ?
+            [NSString stringWithFormat:@"Omarchy is taking long to start. Its logs: %@",
+             [[NSString stringWithUTF8String:logs] stringByAbbreviatingWithTildeInPath]] :
+            @"Omarchy is taking long to start. Its logs are in the VM's folder.";
+        omacvm_splash_hint = [[NSTextField labelWithString:text] retain];
+        [omacvm_splash_hint setFont:[NSFont monospacedSystemFontOfSize:13
+                                                                weight:NSFontWeightRegular]];
+        [omacvm_splash_hint setTextColor:[NSColor colorWithSRGBRed:0.66 green:0.69
+                                                              blue:0.84 alpha:1]];
+        [omacvm_splash_hint sizeToFit];
+        [omacvm_splash_hint setAutoresizingMask:NSViewMinXMargin | NSViewMaxXMargin |
+                                                NSViewMinYMargin | NSViewMaxYMargin];
+    }
+    NSRect b = [cocoaView bounds];
+    NSSize size = [omacvm_splash_hint frame].size;
+    /* 32 points under the logo (in points, from the bottom). */
+    IntroGeom g = omacvm_intro_geom((int)b.size.width, (int)b.size.height);
+    CGFloat y = b.size.height - g.top - g.lh - 32 - size.height;
+    [omacvm_splash_hint setFrame:NSMakeRect(floor((b.size.width - size.width) / 2),
+                                            floor(MAX(8, y)), size.width, size.height)];
+    if (![omacvm_splash_hint superview]) {
+        [cocoaView addSubview:omacvm_splash_hint];
+    }
+}
+
+static int omacvm_splash_seconds(const char *name, int fallback)
+{
+    const char *v = getenv(name);
+    return v && atoi(v) > 0 ? MIN(atoi(v), 3600) : fallback;
+}
+
+static int omacvm_splash_hint_seconds(void)
+{
+    static int seconds;
+    if (!seconds) {
+        seconds = omacvm_splash_seconds("OMACVM_SPLASH_HINT_SECONDS", 90);
+    }
+    return seconds;
+}
+
+/* QEMU's thread, BQL: the guest has run that long and shows nothing yet. */
+static void omacvm_splash_hint_timer(void *opaque)
+{
+    if (omacvm_guest_drew || !omacvm_splash_wanted(gl_scanout_borrow, surface)) {
+        return;
+    }
+    omacvm_splash_hint_up = true;
+    warn_report("cocoa: no picture from the guest %d s after it started",
+                omacvm_splash_hint_seconds());
+    dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
+        omacvm_splash_hint_show(true);
+    });
+}
+
+/* QEMU's thread, BQL: the main output changed. */
+static void omacvm_splash_update(void)
+{
+    omacvm_hold_dirty = true;
+    if (gl_scanout_borrow || (surface && !surface_is_placeholder(surface))) {
+        omacvm_guest_drew = true;
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_guest_drew && omacvm_splash_wanted(gl_scanout_borrow, surface)) {
+        /* Guest time: a paused VM is not slow to start. */
+        if (!omacvm_splash_timer) {
+            omacvm_splash_timer = timer_new_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL,
+                                               omacvm_splash_hint_timer, NULL);
+        }
+        if (!omacvm_splash_hint_up && !timer_pending(omacvm_splash_timer)) {
+            timer_mod(omacvm_splash_timer, qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL) +
+                                           omacvm_splash_hint_seconds() * 1000LL);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+    if (omacvm_splash_timer) {
+        timer_del(omacvm_splash_timer);
+    }
+    if (omacvm_splash_hint_up) {
+        omacvm_splash_hint_up = false;
+        dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
+            omacvm_splash_hint_show(false);
+        });
+    }
+}
+
+/*
+ * With the view context: w x h pixels of the texture from (x, y) (GL's rows,
+ * from the bottom) into px as 0xAARRGGBB. False if it cannot be read (said
+ * once; the logo then waits for the display agent or the time limit).
+ */
+static bool omacvm_splash_read(GLuint tex, int x, int y, int w, int h, uint32_t *px)
+{
+    static GLuint fb;
+    static bool said;
+    GLenum status, err;
+
+    if (!fb) {
+        glGenFramebuffers(1, &fb);
+    }
+    while (glGetError() != GL_NO_ERROR) {
+        /* not ours */
+    }
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER, fb);
+    glFramebufferTexture2D(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER, GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0, GL_TEXTURE_2D, tex, 0);
+    status = glCheckFramebufferStatus(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER);
+    if (status == GL_FRAMEBUFFER_COMPLETE) {
+        glPixelStorei(GL_PACK_ALIGNMENT, 4);
+        glPixelStorei(GL_PACK_ROW_LENGTH, 0);
+        glReadPixels(x, y, w, h, GL_BGRA, GL_UNSIGNED_INT_8_8_8_8_REV, px);
+    }
+    err = glGetError();
+    glFramebufferTexture2D(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER, GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0, GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, 0);
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
+    if (status != GL_FRAMEBUFFER_COMPLETE || err != GL_NO_ERROR) {
+        if (!said) {
+            said = true;
+            info_report("cocoa: boot splash cannot read the guest's picture "
+                        "(framebuffer 0x%x, error 0x%x)", status, err);
+        }
+        return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * QEMU's thread, BQL: does the main output show the guest's desktop? The
+ * probe's pixels, from the GL scanout's texture (one row of it at a time) or
+ * from the 2D surface.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_splash_sees_desktop(void)
+{
+    static uint32_t px[SPLASH_PROBE_ROWS * SPLASH_PROBE_COLS];
+    static uint32_t line[16384];
+
+    if (gl_scanout_borrow) {
+        DisplayGLTexture tex = gl_scanout_borrow(gl_scanout_id);
+        __block bool ok = true;
+
+        if (!tex.width || !tex.height) {
+            tex.width = gl_scanout_x + gl_scanout_w;
+            tex.height = gl_scanout_y + gl_scanout_h;
+        }
+        if (!tex.id || !gl_scanout_w || !gl_scanout_h || tex.width > 16384 ||
+            gl_scanout_x + gl_scanout_w > tex.width || gl_scanout_y + gl_scanout_h > tex.height) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        with_gl_view_ctx(^{
+            for (int r = 0; r < SPLASH_PROBE_ROWS && ok; r++) {
+                int y = gl_scanout_y + omacvm_splash_probe_at(r, SPLASH_PROBE_ROWS, gl_scanout_h);
+                ok = omacvm_splash_read(tex.id, gl_scanout_x, tex.y_0_top ? y : tex.height - 1 - y,
+                                        gl_scanout_w, 1, line);
+                for (int c = 0; ok && c < SPLASH_PROBE_COLS; c++) {
+                    px[r * SPLASH_PROBE_COLS + c] =
+                        line[omacvm_splash_probe_at(c, SPLASH_PROBE_COLS, gl_scanout_w)];
+                }
+            }
+        });
+        return ok && omacvm_splash_desktop(px);
+    }
+    if (!surface || surface_is_placeholder(surface) || surface_bits_per_pixel(surface) != 32) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    for (int r = 0; r < SPLASH_PROBE_ROWS; r++) {
+        const uint8_t *row = (const uint8_t *)surface_data(surface) + (size_t)surface_stride(surface) *
+            omacvm_splash_probe_at(r, SPLASH_PROBE_ROWS, surface_height(surface));
+        for (int c = 0; c < SPLASH_PROBE_COLS; c++) {
+            memcpy(&px[r * SPLASH_PROBE_COLS + c],
+                   row + 4 * omacvm_splash_probe_at(c, SPLASH_PROBE_COLS, surface_width(surface)), 4);
+        }
+    }
+    return omacvm_splash_desktop(px);
+}
+
+/* BQL: has Omarchy's display agent opened its port (it starts with the desktop)? */
+static int omacvm_splash_agent_port(Object *obj, void *opaque)
+{
+    VirtIOSerialPort *port = (VirtIOSerialPort *)object_dynamic_cast(obj, TYPE_VIRTIO_SERIAL_PORT);
+
+    if (port && port->name && !strcmp(port->name, "org.omacvm.display") &&
+        port->guest_connected) {
+        *(bool *)opaque = true;
+        return 1;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static bool omacvm_splash_agent_up(void)
+{
+    const char *chan = getenv("OMACVM_DISPLAY_SOCKET");
+    bool up = false;
+
+    /*
+     * With the window's channel open on the Mac side, the port's opening
+     * proves nothing: the firmware (EDK2's VirtioSerialDxe) opens every port
+     * the host has open, 0.2 s into the boot. Then only the agent's hello counts.
+     */
+    if (chan && *chan) {
+        return qatomic_read(&omacvm_display_hello);
+    }
+    object_child_foreach_recursive(object_get_root(), omacvm_splash_agent_port, &up);
+    return up;
+}
+
+static void omacvm_intro_reveal(bool now);
+
+/*
+ * QEMU's thread, BQL, 4 times a second while the logo waits (10 once the
+ * agent is up): is the desktop there? After the time limit, once a second
+ * until the desktop comes, so that an output it turns off is black.
+ */
+static void omacvm_hold_tick(void *opaque)
+{
+    int64_t now_ms = qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME);
+    int64_t ran = qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL) - omacvm_hold_since;
+    int limit = omacvm_splash_seconds("OMACVM_SPLASH_HOLD_SECONDS", 40);
+    bool error = runstate_check(RUN_STATE_INTERNAL_ERROR) || runstate_check(RUN_STATE_IO_ERROR) ||
+                 runstate_check(RUN_STATE_GUEST_PANICKED);
+    const char *why = NULL;
+    bool lit;
+
+    if (!omacvm_holding && !omacvm_watching) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (omacvm_agent_since < 0 && omacvm_splash_agent_up()) {
+        omacvm_agent_since = now_ms;
+        omacvm_hold_dirty = true;   /* the wallpaper may be there already */
+    }
+    lit = omacvm_hold_dirty && omacvm_splash_sees_desktop();
+    omacvm_hold_dirty = false;
+    if (omacvm_watching) {
+        if (omacvm_agent_since >= 0 || lit) {
+            omacvm_watching = false;
+            omacvm_desktop_up = true;
+            gl_dirty = true;
+            info_report("cocoa: the desktop came after the boot logo's time limit "
+                        "(%.1f s of running time after the start)", ran / 1000.0);
+        } else {
+            timer_mod(omacvm_hold_timer, now_ms + SPLASH_WATCH_TICK_MS);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+    switch (omacvm_splash_look(error, lit, omacvm_agent_since < 0 ? -1 : now_ms - omacvm_agent_since,
+                               ran, limit * 1000LL)) {
+    case SPLASH_LOOK_HOLD:
+        timer_mod(omacvm_hold_timer, now_ms +
+                  (omacvm_agent_since < 0 ? SPLASH_HOLD_TICK_MS : SPLASH_SETTLE_TICK_MS));
+        return;
+    case SPLASH_LOOK_ERROR:
+        why = "the VM stopped on an error";
+        break;
+    case SPLASH_LOOK_DESKTOP:
+        why = omacvm_agent_since < 0 ? "the guest shows its desktop"
+                                     : "Omarchy's display agent started and the desktop is drawn";
+        omacvm_desktop_up = true;
+        break;
+    case SPLASH_LOOK_AGENT:
+        why = "Omarchy's display agent started (no lit desktop 2 s later)";
+        omacvm_desktop_up = true;
+        break;
+    case SPLASH_LOOK_LIMIT:
+        why = "no desktop yet: the guest's screen as it is";
+        omacvm_watching = true;
+        timer_mod(omacvm_hold_timer, now_ms + SPLASH_WATCH_TICK_MS);
+        break;
+    }
+    omacvm_holding = false;
+    gl_dirty = true;
+    info_report("cocoa: boot logo gives way, %s (%.1f s of running time after the start)",
+                why, ran / 1000.0);
+    dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
+        omacvm_intro_reveal(error);
+    });
+}
+
+/* BQL: the window's logo waits for the desktop from now on. */
+static void omacvm_hold_start(void)
+{
+    omacvm_holding = true;
+    omacvm_watching = false;
+    omacvm_hold_dirty = true;
+    omacvm_agent_since = -1;
+    omacvm_hold_since = qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL);
+    if (!omacvm_hold_timer) {
+        omacvm_hold_timer = timer_new_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME, omacvm_hold_tick, NULL);
+    }
+    timer_mod(omacvm_hold_timer, qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME) + SPLASH_HOLD_TICK_MS);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_intro_again(void);
+
+/* A guest reset starts over: the logo again until the desktop, the hint's clock. */
+static void omacvm_splash_reset(void *opaque)
+{
+    omacvm_guest_drew = false;
+    qatomic_set(&omacvm_display_hello, false);
+    omacvm_desktop_up = false;
+    omacvm_watching = false;
+    omacvm_agent_since = -1;
+    if (omacvm_overlay_ok) {
+        omacvm_hold_start();
+        dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
+            omacvm_intro_again();
+        });
+    }
+}
+
+/*
+ * OmacVM start animation: when the window opens, OMACVM turns into Omarchy's
+ * logo (O, M and A stay, the cells of C, V and M fly and land as R, C, H and
+ * Y), Omarchy green on Omarchy's background: OMACVM holds 0.6 s, the cells
+ * fly for about 2.6 s, the glow goes by 3.56 s (omacvm-splash.h has the
+ * timeline). This is the preview the user picked (a-pixel-morph), slowed
+ * down, drawn natively: the cells are a Core Animation shape layer, sharp at
+ * any size, the soft glow a small image under them, worked out as the
+ * preview did. Then the logo holds until the desktop is there (above); if
+ * that comes earlier, the animation still plays to its end, then fades. The
+ * guest is never held up: this is only drawing over the window.
+ * Reduce motion (or OMACVM_SPLASH_ANIMATION=0): the logo without the morph.
+ * After a reboot: the logo, still. Only the main window has it.
+ *
+ * Colours: GL's pixels reach the screen unconverted (the layer has no colour
+ * space), so the layer's green and navy are made in the window's colour space,
+ * and stay the very values of the GL logo, the firmware's and the guest's.
+ *
+ * Threads: all of it runs on the main thread (a CADisplayLink drives the
+ * frames); QEMU's thread only says when to give way (dispatch_async).
+ * The core (the cells at a time, where they go in the window, the glow) is
+ * in ui/omacvm-splash.h: Tests/display/test-boot-splash-morph.c builds and
+ * checks it on its own.
+ */
+
+static void omacvm_splash_colour(uint32_t rgb, CGFloat *c)
+{
+    c[0] = (rgb >> 16) / 255.0;
+    c[1] = ((rgb >> 8) & 0xff) / 255.0;
+    c[2] = (rgb & 0xff) / 255.0;
+    c[3] = 1;
+}
+
+@interface OmacVMIntroLayer : CALayer
+- (id)initStill:(BOOL)still;
+- (void)play;
+- (void)hold;
+- (void)reveal:(BOOL)now;
+@end
+
+static OmacVMIntroLayer *omacvm_intro;   /* main thread; nil once it fades */
+
+#define INTRO_FADE 0.4   /* s */
+
+@implementation OmacVMIntroLayer {
+    CAShapeLayer *cells;
+    CALayer *glow;              /* the glow image over the preview's frame */
+    CADisplayLink *link;
+    CGColorSpaceRef space;      /* the window's */
+    double t;                   /* where the animation is (s) */
+    CFTimeInterval start;       /* of the first frame; 0 before */
+    CFTimeInterval opened;
+    CFTimeInterval last_tick;   /* when the display link last gave a frame; 0 before */
+    bool ready;                 /* the desktop is there: fade once the animation ends */
+    bool fading;
+    IntroCell buf[INTRO_MAX];
+    uint8_t bg[INTRO_BG_W * INTRO_BG_H * 4];
+}
+
+- (id)initStill:(BOOL)still
+{
+    self = [super init];
+    if (self) {
+        NSDictionary *none = @{ @"path": [NSNull null], @"bounds": [NSNull null],
+                                @"position": [NSNull null], @"contents": [NSNull null],
+                                @"contentsScale": [NSNull null], @"hidden": [NSNull null],
+                                @"backgroundColor": [NSNull null], @"fillColor": [NSNull null],
+                                /* -fade's own animation only: CA's implicit 0.25 s one would
+                                 * end first and the logo come back at 25 % for a moment. */
+                                @"opacity": [NSNull null] };
+
+        t = still ? INTRO_END : 0;
+        opened = CACurrentMediaTime();
+        [self setActions:none];
+        /* Under QEMU's labels (pause, the slow-start hint) and the cursor. */
+        [self setZPosition:-1];
+        [self setAutoresizingMask:kCALayerWidthSizable | kCALayerHeightSizable];
+        glow = [[CALayer alloc] init];
+        [glow setActions:none];
+        [glow setContentsGravity:kCAGravityResize];
+        [glow setMagnificationFilter:kCAFilterLinear];
+        [glow setHidden:YES];
+        [self addSublayer:glow];
+        cells = [[CAShapeLayer alloc] init];
+        [cells setActions:none];
+        [cells setAutoresizingMask:kCALayerWidthSizable | kCALayerHeightSizable];
+        [self addSublayer:cells];
+        [self colours];
+        /* Moved to a display with another scale or colour space: draw for it. */
+        [[NSNotificationCenter defaultCenter]
+            addObserver:self selector:@selector(backingChanged:)
+                   name:NSWindowDidChangeBackingPropertiesNotification
+                 object:[cocoaView window]];
+        [[NSNotificationCenter defaultCenter]
+            addObserver:self selector:@selector(backingChanged:)
+                   name:NSWindowDidChangeScreenNotification
+                 object:[cocoaView window]];
+    }
+    return self;
+}
+
+- (void)dealloc
+{
+    [[NSNotificationCenter defaultCenter] removeObserver:self];
+    [cells release];
+    [glow release];
+    CGColorSpaceRelease(space);
+    [super dealloc];
+}
+
+/* Green and navy in the window's colour space, where GL's pixels show unconverted. */
+- (void)colours
+{
+    CGColorSpaceRef s = [[[cocoaView window] colorSpace] CGColorSpace];
+    CGFloat c[4];
+
+    CGColorSpaceRelease(space);
+    space = s ? CGColorSpaceRetain(s) : CGColorSpaceCreateWithName(kCGColorSpaceSRGB);
+    omacvm_splash_colour(SPLASH_NAVY, c);
+    CGColorRef navy = CGColorCreate(space, c);
+    [self setBackgroundColor:navy];
+    CGColorRelease(navy);
+    omacvm_splash_colour(SPLASH_GREEN, c);
+    CGColorRef green = CGColorCreate(space, c);
+    [cells setFillColor:green];
+    CGColorRelease(green);
+}
+
+- (void)backingChanged:(NSNotification *)n
+{
+    [self colours];
+    [self render];
+}
+
+/* The frame at t, at the layer's size now. */
+- (void)render
+{
+    CGRect b = [self bounds];
+    CGFloat scale = [[cocoaView window] backingScaleFactor];
+    double strength;
+    int n = omacvm_intro_cells(t, buf, &strength);
+    int w = (int)(b.size.width * scale), h = (int)(b.size.height * scale);
+
+    if (w < 1 || h < 1 || scale <= 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    IntroGeom g = omacvm_intro_geom(w, h);
+    CGMutablePathRef path = CGPathCreateMutable();
+    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        double e[4];
+        omacvm_intro_rect(&g, &buf[i], e);
+        /* The layer counts from the bottom, in points. */
+        CGPathAddRect(path, NULL, CGRectMake(e[0] / scale, (h - e[3]) / scale,
+                                             (e[2] - e[0]) / scale, (e[3] - e[1]) / scale));
+    }
+
+    [CATransaction begin];
+    [CATransaction setDisableActions:YES];
+    [cells setFrame:b];
+    [cells setContentsScale:scale];
+    [cells setPath:path];
+    if (strength > 0) {
+        /* The preview's frame, scaled so that its logo lies on the window's. */
+        double sx = g.sx / INTRO_PX, sy = g.sy / INTRO_PX;
+        double top = g.top - INTRO_LOGO_Y * sy;
+
+        omacvm_intro_background(buf, n, strength, bg);
+        CFDataRef bytes = CFDataCreate(NULL, bg, sizeof(bg));
+        CGDataProviderRef data = CGDataProviderCreateWithCFData(bytes);
+        CGImageRef image = CGImageCreate(INTRO_BG_W, INTRO_BG_H, 8, 32, INTRO_BG_W * 4,
+                                         space, (CGBitmapInfo)kCGImageAlphaNoneSkipLast,
+                                         data, NULL, true, kCGRenderingIntentDefault);
+        [glow setFrame:CGRectMake((g.left - INTRO_LOGO_X * sx) / scale,
+                                  (h - top - INTRO_H * sy) / scale,
+                                  INTRO_W * sx / scale, INTRO_H * sy / scale)];
+        [glow setContents:(id)image];
+        [glow setHidden:NO];
+        CGImageRelease(image);
+        CGDataProviderRelease(data);
+        CFRelease(bytes);
+    } else {
+        [glow setContents:nil];
+        [glow setHidden:YES];
+    }
+    [CATransaction commit];
+    CGPathRelease(path);
+}
+
+- (void)layoutSublayers
+{
+    [super layoutSublayers];
+    [self render];
+}
+
+- (void)play
+{
+    if (t >= INTRO_END) {
+        [self render];
+        return;
+    }
+    link = [cocoaView displayLinkWithTarget:self selector:@selector(tick:)];
+    [link addToRunLoop:[NSRunLoop mainRunLoop] forMode:NSRunLoopCommonModes];
+}
+
+- (void)fade
+{
+    CABasicAnimation *a = [CABasicAnimation animationWithKeyPath:@"opacity"];
+    CFTimeInterval now = [self convertTime:CACurrentMediaTime() fromLayer:nil];
+
+    if (fading) {
+        return;
+    }
+    fading = true;
+    [link invalidate];   /* it holds us */
+    link = nil;
+    if (omacvm_intro == self) {
+        omacvm_intro = nil;   /* a reset from now on gets a new logo */
+    }
+    info_report("cocoa: boot logo fades into the guest's screen, %.2f s after it came up",
+                CACurrentMediaTime() - opened);
+    [a setFromValue:@1.0];
+    [a setToValue:@0.0];
+    [a setBeginTime:now];
+    [a setDuration:INTRO_FADE];
+    [a setFillMode:kCAFillModeBackwards];
+    [a setTimingFunction:[CAMediaTimingFunction
+                          functionWithName:kCAMediaTimingFunctionEaseInEaseOut]];
+    [CATransaction begin];
+    [CATransaction setCompletionBlock:^{
+        [self removeFromSuperlayer];
+        [self release];   /* the alloc in omacvm_intro_show */
+    }];
+    [self addAnimation:a forKey:@"fade"];
+    [self setOpacity:0];
+    [CATransaction commit];
+}
+
+- (void)tick:(CADisplayLink *)l
+{
+    CFTimeInterval now = [l targetTimestamp];
+
+    last_tick = CACurrentMediaTime();
+    if (!start) {
+        start = now;
+    }
+    t = now - start;
+    if (t >= INTRO_END) {
+        t = INTRO_END;
+        [link invalidate];
+        link = nil;
+        if (ready) {
+            [self fade];
+        }
+    }
+    [self render];
+}
+
+/* The guest was reset before the logo faded: wait for the desktop again. */
+- (void)hold
+{
+    ready = false;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Ready, and the display link still runs the animation: it fades at the
+ * animation's end. A window that is not visible gets no frames from it
+ * (another Space, hidden), so once the animation is over by the clock and
+ * no frame came for a while, fade without it: else the logo would stay over
+ * the desktop until the window shows again.
+ */
+- (void)fadeIfStalled
+{
+    CFTimeInterval left = opened + INTRO_END - CACurrentMediaTime();
+
+    if (!ready || fading || !link) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (left <= 0 && CACurrentMediaTime() - last_tick > 0.25) {
+        info_report("cocoa: boot logo: the animation got no frames for a while, fading without it");
+        [self fade];
+        return;
+    }
+    [self retain];
+    dispatch_after(dispatch_time(DISPATCH_TIME_NOW, (int64_t)(MAX(left, 0.25) * NSEC_PER_SEC)),
+                   dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
+        [self fadeIfStalled];
+        [self release];
+    });
+}
+
+/* The desktop is there (or the logo gives way): fade after the animation; now: at once. */
+- (void)reveal:(BOOL)now
+{
+    ready = true;
+    if (now || !link) {
+        [self fade];
+        return;
+    }
+    [self fadeIfStalled];
+}
+@end
+
+/* Main thread: put the logo's layer over the window (still: without the morph). */
+static void omacvm_intro_show(bool still)
+{
+    omacvm_intro = [[OmacVMIntroLayer alloc] initStill:still];
+    [omacvm_intro setFrame:[[cocoaView layer] bounds]];
+    [[cocoaView layer] addSublayer:omacvm_intro];
+    [omacvm_intro play];
+}
+
+/* Main thread: the guest was reset: the logo, still, until its desktop. */
+static void omacvm_intro_again(void)
+{
+    if (omacvm_intro) {
+        [omacvm_intro hold];
+    } else {
+        omacvm_intro_show(true);
+    }
+}
+
+/* Main thread: the logo gives way (now: at once, even mid-animation). */
+static void omacvm_intro_reveal(bool now)
+{
+    [omacvm_intro reveal:now];
+}
+
+/* Main thread, with the BQL (cocoa_display_init): start the animation. */
+static void omacvm_intro_start(void)
+{
+    const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_SPLASH_ANIMATION");
+    bool reduce = [[NSWorkspace sharedWorkspace] accessibilityDisplayShouldReduceMotion];
+    bool off = v && !strcmp(v, "0");
+
+    if (!omacvm_splash_enabled() || getenv("OMACVM_COCOA_HIDDEN") ||
+        !(cocoa_gl_present_on() ||
+          [[cocoaView layer] isKindOfClass:[CAOpenGLLayer class]])) {
+        return;
+    }
+    info_report("cocoa: start animation %s", reduce ? "still (Reduce motion)" :
+                off ? "still (OMACVM_SPLASH_ANIMATION=0)" : "on");
+    omacvm_overlay_ok = true;
+    omacvm_intro_show(reduce || off);
+    omacvm_hold_start();
+}
